From c909e4f4976ab37cd41f3d98ec7f537cfb08760b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:25:20 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 40/47] scripting: effect and shader-constant scripts,
 getAnimation, media event order

- A script on an effect's `visible` has thisObject = that effect
  (IEffect), as WE's IThisPropertyObject is the property's owner.
  thisObject was the layer, so `thisObject.visible = e.hasThumbnail`
  hid the whole layer.
- Scripts on an effect's shader constants (constantshadervalues) are
  queued and run like a layer property's (the audit's S4, for
  effects): album-cover fades, audio pulses on uniforms.
- getAnimation (name?) on a layer: the keyframe animation of the
  property whose script runs now (thisObject.getAnimation () in a
  property script), else of a property or effect constant of the
  layer, by name. IAnimation: play (a finished `single` one from the
  start), pause, stop (to the start, paused), isPlaying, getFrame,
  setFrame, name, frameCount, fps, duration. A change shows on the
  same frame.
- Queued media events reach scripts in a fixed order: status,
  properties, thumbnail, playback, timeline (a playback handler may
  print the title it was just given; std::map order sent playback
  first).

Origin: ours
Why: scripted "now playing" covers stayed hidden or black (docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B10: S26 getAnimation, S11, S4 for effects)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
